(Title) Tj
T*
(Twenty-Four-Hour Intraocular Pressure Response to Sepetaprost Compared With Latanoprost in) Tj
T*
(Glaucoma Patients) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Sepetaprost represents a novel prostaglandin formulation with potential therapeutic) Tj
T*
(benefits for glaucoma management. In this exploratory trial, 33 adults with glaucoma or) Tj
T*
(ocular hypertension received either sepetaprost \(n=17\) or latanoprost \(n=16\) daily for 12) Tj
T*
(weeks. At the end of treatment, mean 24-hour intraocular pressure was numerically lower in) Tj
T*
(the sepetaprost group relative to latanoprost, though this difference did not achieve) Tj
T*
(statistical significance at the pre-specified threshold. Nocturnal intraocular pressure) Tj
T*
(measurements demonstrated a trend toward lower values with sepetaprost. Both agents) Tj
T*
(reduced intraocular pressure from baseline by approximately 5-7 mmHg. Adverse events were) Tj
T*
(frequent in both groups, occurring in the majority of participants. Safety profiles were) Tj
T*
(comparable between the two treatments. These findings suggest sepetaprost warrants further) Tj
T*
(investigation in adequately powered studies to clarify its role in glaucoma management.) Tj
ET
